From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 20:50:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add inline-span box decorations to text layout

Extend TextStyle / StyleProperty / ResolvedStyle / layout::Style with
box-decoration fields (padding-inline, border-inline width + brush,
background_brush, border_radius). Span enter/leave advance is charged
as spacing gaps (like letter spacing) so spans contribute to line width
like real CSS inline boxes, and break candidates are anchored so
trailing decorations don't orphan onto the next line. A per-line
span-fragment sidecar tells the painter where to draw the decorations.

Without this, button-styled <a>/<span> elements inside inline-flow
containers (todomvc filter pills, "Clear completed", any styled inline
link) render as plain text.
